WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.885
A hardcoded string is user-facing
text in code that skips i18n,

2
00:00:05.885 --> 00:00:08.102
so every locale shows
the source language.

3
00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:11.729
Add a linter in CI that
fails on each new one.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.587
General Translation lints the
text inside &lt;T&gt; and can wrap

5
00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:16.816
the text outside it.

6
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.630
Pair no-literal-string with
@generaltranslation/react-core-linter,

7
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.846
and exclude &lt;T&gt; from that rule.

8
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.679
Locadex's Generate code
automation wraps untranslated text

9
00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:32.268
and opens a pull request.

10
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.690
In a pseudo-locale, wrapped
text turns accented and missed

11
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.094
text stays plain.

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.190
Your team now ships every screen
translated with each release.
